The root cause is clear now: `nr_bench --count` never increments its single-op count variable, so PF-2’s count-mode run can hang until the outer timeout kills it. I’m going to patch PF-2 to use a one-second rate-capped measured window by default and add an upper-bound check so stale million-sample results cannot still pass.
