+Round 2 summary:
+
+- FN-2 stayed fixed; the evidence still reports measured wait (`等待 4.0s`) instead of the configured max.
+- FN-4 passed twice again; compression and dedup stats both increased on consecutive runs.
+- PF-2 was repaired in the live path. `nr_bench` count-mode was not actually bounded for single-op PUTs, so I switched PF-2 to a short rate-capped measured window and added a hard upper bound. Live sample count now lands at `102285`, with avg `37.67us`, p99 `63.61us`, no fail/degraded.
+- PF-4 initially failed on scenario B at `106.05ms` / `114.71ms`. I optimized `nr_bench` count-mode to defer per-op atomic bookkeeping, then reran PF-4 with the existing measured logic. It now passes with scenario B at `97.53ms`.
+- PF-5 passed live with the bounded 1s batch window.
+- PF-6 remained the only open issue. Multiple bounded reruns still failed, with either write-side fail/degraded collapse or low-hit read behavior after the 1MB slab restart. The last live run ended at `write_gbs=6.435`, `read_gbs=16.284`, `read_hit_ratio=0.8933`.
+- PF-7 presentation output is correct: visible result summary shows only `P999=846.096us`, and strict RAID5 confirmation stays separate (`strict_acceptance_passed=false` when `RAID5_CONFIRMED` is unset).
